  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>atracurium</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>M03AC04</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, IV dosing <small>(PK_1C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Fisher DM et al. 1990</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>infants, children, and adults</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>atracurium</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_atracurium/Atracurium_Fisher1990_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>Volume of distribution at steady state</td><td>210</td><td>ml/kg</td><td><small>Vss</small></td></tr><tr><td>total clearance</td><td>7.9</td><td>ml.kg-1.min-1</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>elimination half-life</td><td>20.0</td><td>min</td><td><small>t1/2z</small></td></tr><tr><td>volume of distribution</td><td>4.7</td><td>L/kg</td><td><small>V</small></td></tr></table><h4>About atracurium</h4><p>Atracurium is a muscle relaxant used to relax muscles during surgery and to help with insertion of a breathing tube under anaesthesia. It is widely used in anaesthetic practice and appears on the WHO list of essential medicines.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q165660\">Wikidata Q165660</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Atracurium\">Atracurium</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Fisher DM et al. (1990). Pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics of atracurium in infants and children. <i>Anesthesiology 73(1):33–37</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1097/00000542-199007000-00006\">10.1097/00000542-199